cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. When you report a
  measurement, cite the DOI of the version you actually ran rather than the
  concept DOI — the tool's own report records which version produced it, and a
  citation that does not pin the version cannot be checked against that record.
title: "closure_drift: does your version label name exactly one version of your code?"
abstract: >-
  A read-only, zero-dependency tool that measures, over any git repository,
  whether a declared version label identifies exactly one state of the code at
  the points where that repository publishes. 0.9.0 corrects the detector after
  an audit (files with non-ASCII names and submodule pointers were outside the
  closure; undetermined results exited 0), adds a check to run before tagging,
  and ships three pre-registered test batteries. Exit 0 means clean and nothing
  else. Each report stamps the commit measured and the hash of the tool.
